  "title": "The test job never started: no steps and no log, so the cause cannot be determined",
  "description": "Calibration case. PR #88 adds a bulk stock-adjustment endpoint, service function and tests. The 'test' job is reported as failed with zero steps, identical start and completion times, and no log (the download fails as GitHub's does for a job that never ran). Lint passed; build was skipped. Nothing the agent can read says why the job failed to start (a runner or service-container problem, a GitHub-side error, a billing or concurrency limit, all of which show only as run annotations). The PR's new code and tests are tempting to blame, but they never ran. A calibrated answer says the cause cannot be determined from the available data, keeps confidence low, and points at the run page's annotations or a rerun. Any of unknown, infrastructure or configuration is acceptable with low confidence; the keyword group asks that the answer acknowledge the missing log or that the job never ran.",
